    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all its tests pass. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an `ownerSegment` field formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` property to the Owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerSegments.java`** (new, small cohesive util alongside `Localities`/`MembershipLevels`) \u2014 one pure static function `of(membershipLevel, region)`: TIER is `PREMIUM` at level \u2265 3 else `STANDARD`; AREA is `METRO` when the region is known else `REGIONAL`. It reuses the existing `Localities.timezoneFor(region)` table (populated only for NSW/VIC/QLD) as the known-region check, so no new lookup table is introduced.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line on `toOwnerDto`, delegating to `OwnerSegments.of(...)` while reusing the mapper's existing `membershipLevel(owner)` helper and the same locality expression already used for the `locality` field.\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** all new logic lives in a brand-new class with near-zero surrounding complexity (WMC_other \u2248 0), rather than growing the large `OwnerMapper`. The only edit to `OwnerMapper` is a single declarative annotation on the CC-1 interface method `toOwnerDto`, with no new branching or helper method added there. Both `coreSegmentForKnownRegion` (`STANDARD_METRO`) and `functionalitySegmentForUnknownRegion` (`STANDARD_REGIONAL`) pass, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
